--TEST--
`is tainted string` and `is secret bytes` are refused, because both qualifiers are erased before codegen and no value carries one at run time (`rule:types/type-test`, `rule:security/tainted-qualifier`, `rule:security/secret-qualifier`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The second of `rule:types/type-test`'s three refusals, and the one that is
// not about the answer being knowable. `tainted` and `secret` are decided
// where a value is declared and erased before codegen, so a tag comparison
// has nothing to read — the question has no answer at all, which is why it
// is refused where `is int` over an `int` local is not.
mixed $m = "ab";
echo $m is tainted string, "\n";
echo $m is secret bytes, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0813]: `tainted string` is a qualifier the compiler erases, so no value carries it at run time
%A
error[E0813]: `secret bytes` is a qualifier the compiler erases, so no value carries it at run time
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
